IRO is free. You do not need to pay for it, and nothing is locked.

1. Use. You may install and use IRO on as many computers as you like, for personal work and for paid client work.

2. Source code. You may read and study the source code, change it for your own use, and send changes back to this repository. By sending a change, you agree that it may be included in IRO under this licence. Forking this repository on GitHub to propose changes is fine.

3. Sharing. You may share the unmodified installer, or a link to this repository, as long as you do not charge for it.

4. What you may not do. You may not sell IRO or a modified version of it, include it in a paid product, publish a modified version as a separate product or under another name, or present it as your own work.

5. Name and logo. The IRO name and logo belong to the author and are not licensed for any other use.

6. Donations are voluntary. They are a thank-you and do not unlock anything.

7. Privacy. IRO reads the audio files you choose, on your own computer, to sort and preview them. It does not upload your files or send anything about you anywhere. You are responsible for holding the rights to the sounds you use.

8. Blackmagic Design. IRO runs inside DaVinci Resolve Studio, which is a product of Blackmagic Design and is licensed separately. IRO is not made, endorsed or supported by Blackmagic Design. This repository does not include any Blackmagic files.

9. No warranty. IRO is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind. The author is not liable for any loss of data, time or business arising from its use, to the extent the law allows.
